# Nixon — macOS Developer ID signing + notarization credentials.
#
# Copy to `.env.signing` (gitignored) and fill in. When present, `release.sh`
# sources this file and `tauri build` (via build-gpu.sh) signs with your
# Developer ID and notarizes + staples the DMG, producing a build that opens
# from a normal internet/browser download. When absent, the build falls back to
# ad-hoc signing (install via `gh release download`). See ADR-0008 + SETUP.md.
#
# Prereqs (one-time): Apple Developer Program membership; a "Developer ID
# Application" cert + private key in your login keychain; notarization creds
# (App Store Connect API key, recommended — or an app-specific password).
# Verify the cert is present:  security find-identity -v -p codesigning

# --- signing identity (required to leave ad-hoc) ---------------------------
# Exact name as shown by `security find-identity -v -p codesigning`.
APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: Your Name (TEAMID)"

# --- notarization: pick ONE of the two blocks below ------------------------

# (A) App Store Connect API key — preferred (works headless / CI).
#     App Store Connect → Users and Access → Integrations → App Store Connect
#     API → generate a key with the "Developer" role. Download the .p8 ONCE.
APPLE_API_ISSUER="00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"   # Issuer ID (UUID)
APPLE_API_KEY="XXXXXXXXXX"                                  # Key ID
APPLE_API_KEY_PATH="/absolute/path/to/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8"

# (B) Apple ID + app-specific password (simpler, interactive-ish). Comment out
#     block (A) if you use this one.
# APPLE_ID="you@example.com"
# APPLE_PASSWORD="abcd-efgh-ijkl-mnop"   # app-specific password from appleid.apple.com
# APPLE_TEAM_ID="TEAMID"
